> the S-plus function choleski() -- the Fortran function that 
> it calls does 
> not appear to be affected by the deviations from the 
> symmetric that are in 
> the result of t(x) %*% x.  The interface to choleski() is 
> different than 
> chol(), but it's not that difficult to cope with.
> 
> The other fix is to make the result of z <- t(x) %*% x 
