  But remember those functions only convert the name of the object that was
passed.  If a function calls another function passing those data, the name
that deparse(substitute()) returns is the name of the variable in the
calling program.  For example:

func1 <- function(x)
  print(func2(x))
func2 <- function(y)
  deparse(substitute(y))
